# Reasoned suppressions — each entry names WHY the rule does not apply here, so the
# remaining lint output stays a check that can pass.
#
# WRITING/ai-trope:harness: "agent harness" is the product's core technical
# vocabulary (harness independence is a constitutional property, docs/02 and
# ADR-0002), not an AI-trope filler word. Scoped to the surfaces that use it
# technically.
WRITING/ai-trope:harness:README.md
WRITING/ai-trope:harness:docs/**

# WHY: the hybrid-gate reusable workflow is called as @main BY FLEET DESIGN —
# forkwright/.github is operator-owned, so the supply-chain surface the
# unpinned-action rule guards is the fleet itself, and @main is the deliberate
# single-update channel that propagates gate fixes to every caller repo.
# Matches every other adopting repo's suppression (e.g. harmonia).
SHELL/unpinned-action:.github/workflows/gate-attestation.yml

# WHY: hybrid-gate.yml (forkwright/.github) already declares
# `concurrency: group: ${{ github.workflow }}-...` and its own comment states
# a caller must NOT also set a concurrency group with that same key, or the
# shared group self-cancels every adopting repo's runs against each other.
# A caller-side concurrency block here would be the bug this rule exists to
# catch, not the fix for it.
YAML/missing-concurrency:.github/workflows/gate-attestation.yml
